From b4cc3ee0ac1fd5fca773dc1d876c9f0de24f0d15 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cheyenne Wills <cwills@sinenomine.net>
Date: Tue, 7 Jul 2026 15:53:16 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] linux: replace strncpy with strscpy

The Linux 7.2 commit:
    'string: Remove strncpy() from the kernel' (079a028d6327e)
removed the strncpy() function.

As a replacement, we can use the strscpy() function that was introduced
by the Linux 4.3 commit:
    'string: provide strscpy()' (30035e45753b7)

strncpy() is only used on LINUX in the macro osi_procname(), and
osi_procname() is only used to log the process name with afs_warn().
We don't need the NUL-padding behavior or the return value of strncpy(),
so using strscpy() as a drop-in replacement for strncpy() is fine.

Add a configure test to verify that strscpy is available in the Linux
kernel headers and update the 'osi_procname' macro to use strscpy()
instead of strncpy() when it is available.

Note, since strscpy() was introduced in Linux 4.3, this commit is
retroactive.

Reviewed-on: https://gerrit.openafs.org/16872
Tested-by: BuildBot <buildbot@rampaginggeek.com>
Reviewed-by: Michael Meffie <mmeffie@sinenomine.net>
Reviewed-by: Andrew Deason <adeason@sinenomine.net>
Reviewed-by: Marcio Brito Barbosa <mbarbosa@sinenomine.net>
